    {
      "id": "f711194",
      "title": "security-guidance: remove stash indexes older releases left in the git directory",
      "date": "2026-10-07T15:40:40Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/commit/f711194a9ecdf004b655dbc5006610fbb9e7c7bb",
      "snippet": "Releases before 2.0.10 ran `git stash create` on the real index. When that git was killed, it left an `index.stash.<pid>` file the size of the index in the git directory, and nothing removes those: a clone can hold hundreds.  Before it copies the index, the hook now deletes such files once they are ",
      "source": "gh-commits-plugins-official",
      "sourceCategory": "community",
      "sourceName": "anthropics/claude-plugins-official (main commits)",
      "uniqueKey": "f711194|gh-commits-plugins-official"
    },
    {
      "id": "bfe2164",
      "title": "security-guidance: stop a killed hook from leaving index copies behind (2.0.10 → 2.0.11)",
      "date": "2026-10-07T15:35:56Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/commit/bfe21649b9ccdbc67599d6647ff139a4c34e4458",
      "snippet": "In a clone with a very large git index, 2.0.10 could still fill the disk. It copies the index for each git call that might write it, and a hook that Claude Code cancels (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL) never reached its cleanup, so every cancelled hook left index-sized files in the temp directory for up to 3",
      "source": "gh-commits-plugins-official",
      "sourceCategory": "community",
      "sourceName": "anthropics/claude-plugins-official (main commits)",
      "uniqueKey": "bfe2164|gh-commits-plugins-official"
